# Intentionally empty. Do not add entries.
#
# This file is root-level and applies to every image CI scans. Until
# 2026-11-03 it held five advisories accepted on 2026-08-04 for the
# published caddy:2-alpine binary; the frontend has rebuilt Caddy from
# source since 2026-09-11 (frontend/Dockerfile), and three of the five
# were Go standard-library advisories that could equally have hidden a
# real finding in the `culprit` CLI image, which is a Go binary. They were
# removed in Phase 31.1 (docs/DIAGNOSTIC_PLAN.md), once fail-fast: false
# meant every image is scanned in the same run.
#
# If an image's scan goes red, fix the image: bump the dependency, the
# base image, or the Caddy pins (docs/LIMITS.md, "The dashboard's Caddy is
# built from source"). An accepted vulnerability is a decision for the
# architecture session (docs/HANDOFF.md §6), not a line in this file.
